course: dictionary
lesson: 15872
title: Unhook: taking things off hooks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word unhook is made of two parts: un- and hook. The un- part often means undo or reverse, so unhook means to take something off a hook or to undo a hook.
explain: «Dad unhooked the coat from the peg and put it on.» Here the coat was hanging on a hook, and now it is free. Test your meaning: if you swap in "took off the hook", the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Fishers unhook fish gently and put them back in the water. «She unhooked the little fish carefully and let it swim away.» The word tells you the hook must come out without harming the fish.
explain: Unhook can also mean undoing the tiny hooks on a dress, or separating a trailer from the car that pulls it. The other words in the sentence show you which meaning is being used.
fact: Unhook means to take something off a hook, or to undo a hook.
fact: The prefix un- often means undo or reverse, as in unlock, untie and unhook.
fact: Unhook is a verb, so it changes: unhooks, unhooked, unhooking.
fact: «Unhook» can mean undoing the small hooks on a dress, as well as taking a hook out of something.
fact: A trailer can be unhooked from a car, which means the two are no longer joined together.
exercise: «Mum unhooked the dog's lead from the gate.» What does unhooked mean? | Ran away fast | Tied a knot in the lead | Painted the gate | *Took the lead off a hook
exercise: «The fisherman carefully unhooked the fish and let it go.» What is the fisherman doing? | Feeding the fish to the birds | Cooking the fish | Catching a second fish | *Taking the hook out of the fish
exercise: «The farmer unhooked the trailer before driving the tractor to the shed.» What did the farmer separate? | *The trailer from the tractor | The gate from the fence | The hay from the barn | The tractor from the field
test: «Sam unhooked the gate and walked through into the garden.» What did Sam do to the gate? | Locked it shut for ever | Painted it | Climbed over it | *Lifted it off its hook so it could open
test: The prefix un- often means what? | Again and again | Very big | *Undo or reverse | Under the ground
exam: «Maya unhooked her dress at the back before she went to bed.» What did Maya do to her dress? | Washed the dress | *Undid the small hooks on the dress | Hung the dress outside to dry | Sewed a new hook on the dress
